ew file, so the solution.py will have this function. Let me make sure the code is correct.\n\nAnother thing: the problem says the function should take two integers. So the parameters are a and b, both integers. The function returns an integer.\n\nSo the code would be:\n\ndef find_angle(a, b):\n    """Calculate the third angle of a triangle given the other two."""\n    return 180 - a - b\n\nYes, that\'s it. I think that\'s all. Let me check if there are any edge cases. For example, if a or b is zero, but the problem probably assumes they are valid angles. So the function works as intended.\n</think>\n\n```python\n# Solution to find the third angle of a triangle given two angles\n\ndef find_angle(a, b):\n    """Calculate the third angle of a triangle given the other two."""\n    return 180 - a - b\n```'
